/-!
# `H²(Π̂_{g,0}, ℤ/n) ≅ ℤ/n` and the synchronization `M_X ≅ I_x` ([AbsTopIII], Proposition 1.4)

[AbsTopIII], Proposition 1.4 (l.1752–1806 of
`~/iut-scratch/papers/txt/Topics in Absolute Anabelian Geometry III.txt`):

* (i) (l.1764–1770) "the inertia group `I_x` of `x` in `Δ_U` is naturally isomorphic to `Ẑ(1)`;
  the kernels of the natural surjections `Δ_U ↠ Δ_{U_x}` […] are topologically normally
  generated by the inertia groups of points of `U_x \ U`";
* (ii) (l.1771–1801) "we have a natural exact sequence `1 → I_x → Δ^{c-cn}_{U_x} → Δ_X → 1`
  […] applying the differential of the "`E₂`-term" of the Leray spectral sequence associated to
  this group extension to the element `1 ∈ Ẑ = Hom(I_x, I_x)` […] yields an element
  `∈ H²(Δ_X, H⁰(I_x, I_x)) = Hom(M_X, I_x)` — where we write `M_X = Hom(H²(Δ_X, Ẑ), Ẑ)` […];
  this last element corresponds to the natural isomorphism `M_X ≅ I_x`".

Here `Δ_{U_x}` (the curve `X` of genus `g` minus one point) is the free profinite group on
`a₁, b₁, …, a_g, b_g`, the cusp inertia is generated by `∏ᵢ ⁅aᵢ, bᵢ⁆` and filling the cusp gives
the closed surface group `Δ_X = Π̂_{g,0}`. In this file:

* `Fhat g` is the profinite completion of the free group on `Fin g ⊕ Fin g` (`a_i = inl i`,
  `b_i = inr i`), `rel g = ∏ᵢ ⁅aᵢ, bᵢ⁆`, `relSub g` the closed normal subgroup generated by it,
  and **`SurfGrp g = Fhat g ⧸ relSub g`**, the profinite closed surface group `Π̂_{g,0}`;
* `cuspInertia (surfMap g)` is the kernel `I` of `Δ^{c-cn} → Π̂_{g,0}` (`CuspTransgression`);
  it is topologically generated by the class `relBar g` of the relation (`cuspInertia_le`);
* **the transgression is bijective**: `cuspTg : Hom_cont(I, A) → H²(Δ^{c-cn}/I, A)` is injective
  for every discrete abelian `A` (`cuspTg_injective`: a homomorphism on `Δ^{c-cn}` kills the
  product of commutators) and surjective for finite `A` (`cuspTg_surjective`: inflation to
  `Δ^{c-cn}` kills every class, by lifting the free generators to the twisted product
  `A ×_c Π̂_{g,0}`); `cuspTgEquiv`;
* for `g ≥ 1`, the Heisenberg group mod `n` shows that `relBar g` has order `n` modulo every
  `n`, hence `Hom_cont(I, ℤ/n) ≅ ℤ/n` by evaluation at `relBar g` (`inertiaHomEquiv`), and
  **`h2SurfEquiv : H²(Π̂_{g,0}, ℤ/n) ≅ ℤ/n`** (`H²` of `Δ^{c-cn}/I ≃ₜ* Π̂_{g,0}`);
* Proposition 1.4(i) for this model: **`inertiaEquiv : Ẑ ≃ₜ* I`**, `1 ↦ relBar g`;
* Proposition 1.4(ii): with `M_X = lim_n Hom(H²(Δ_X, ℤ/n), ℤ/n)` (`MX`), **`syncEquiv : I ≃* M_X`**,
  `i ↦ (z ↦ (d₂⁻¹ z)(i))` — the isomorphism determined by the transgression `d₂` of
  `1 ∈ Hom(I, I)` (at finite level `cuspClass`).

The identification of the geometric `Δ_{U_x}` with `Fhat g` and of `I_x` with the cusp inertia is
`curves-jacobian`/`pi1` material (`Δ_U ≃ Π̂_{g,r}`); `pi1`'s `Π̂_{g,0}` (`SurfaceGroup g 0`, not in
the `pi1` revision iut pins) is the profinite completion of the discrete one-relator group, which
is `SurfGrp g` by the universal properties (bridge left for the pin bump).
-/

